// DEF-359 + DEF-360 + DEF-361 + DEF-362 (landing 169): THE FOUR FACES OF THE SPAWN READERS THAT MANAGEMENT'S
// REVIEW OF LANDING 168 FOUND, each a hole on landing 167 and landing 168 alike.
//
// A pick EXPRESSION standing as a spawned method's RECEIVER, or inside a SANCTIONED pointer argument of a
// spawn, was entered by neither spawn reader of the escape pass -- `escape_spawn_recv` judged the receiver's
// crossing and never walked it, and `escape_spawn_args`' sanctioned `continue` skipped `escape_expr` -- so a
// view its arm declared recorded no ref and the arm's write of the viewed root was silent (DEF-359; the task
// read the freed bytes, 113/114 at both legs). A by-value `self` method spawned THROUGH A POINTER crossed
// unrefused: `rxt` was the pointer's type, which drops nothing (DEF-360; 109/109) -- and the spawn's child frame
// is built from the receiver EXPRESSION's words, the POINTER's, not the pointee's, so the task reads a WRONG
// VALUE even where nothing is written (DEF-363, the emitter's face, which the AWAIT shares -- `emit_child_frame`
// builds both frames: `drop pp.lookp()` and `await pp.lookp()` over plain data, nothing written, 114 at both legs
// on 168 and 169; `(<-pp).lookp()`, spawned or awaited, and the by-name spelling copy the pointee and are right).
// A generic `T` instantiated at an owner crossed by value: `type_drops` has no answer for a `TY_PARAM`, and the
// instance at `string` is never asked (DEF-361; the copy is the hazard). And the TRAIT-QUALIFIED spawn
// `drop Tr.m(w, n)` handed the trait's NAME to the receiver reader (its type 0: nothing judged) and set
// `pos_base` to 1, so every argument was judged by the NEXT parameter's mode -- the owner `w` admitted, and a
// legal `move` argument refused by a parameter that does not exist (DEF-362; f4c, and f4d the over-refusal
// landing 168 introduced, its legal half control 11). NOW the receiver and the sanctioned argument are WALKED
// before their crossing is judged (sites 1-3: NITPICK-BORROW-015 at the write inside the arm); a by-value
// receiver reached THROUGH A POINTER crosses the spawn AS THAT POINTER and is refused whatever the pointee's
// type, the closed direction (DEF-54) until the child-frame builder dereferences it (sites 4-6 the owner
// pointee -- site 6 with nothing written --, sites 14-16 PLAIN DATA: a pointer local with the owner writing,
// nothing written, an inline address; each NITPICK-BORROW-004 at the receiver; `drop (<-pp).lookp()` and a copy
// into a local are the legal half's controls 4 and 5); a `TY_PARAM` argument is an
// OWNER to the by-value rule, the closed direction (DEF-54), so it crosses only into a `move` parameter (sites
// 7-8: `-004` at the argument; site 9 the `T: Copy` instance -- a licensed copy (D-327) refused here because the
// escape pass reaches no bound table, KNOWN, 0 tree sites by the sweep, the relaxation owed with a bound table
// reachable from the pass); and a method-call operand with NO type is a QUALIFIER -- no receiver, `pos_base` 0,
// so `w` is parameter 0's by-value `Self:self` (sites 10-12: `-004` at `w`, at the temporary, and at `w` ALONE
// where the `move` argument beside it is legal; site 13 a trait-qualified POINTER receiver, `drop Tp.mp(@w)`,
// `-004` at the argument as `drop w.mp()` is at its receiver). Landing 168's checker reports exactly TWO sites of
// this file -- site 12 at the WRONG argument, `move(s2)` (the shift), and site 13 at `@w` by the same rule and
// text as here (the shift judged the address by parameter 1's mode, a pointer either way) -- and none of the
// others; the legal half is tests/backend/programs/spawn_review_faces_ok.npk. The cells:
// wt/51a/.internal/probes/t168/rev168/cells_all4/ (f1a-f1c, f2a-f2b, f3a, f3c, f4a-f4e) and t169/cells_r/,
// cells_r2/ (r1-r14, the receiver's spellings at the spawn and under `await`).
// LANDING 170 (2026-10-30): the child-frame seed loads the pointee (DEF-363), so a by-value receiver reached
// through a pointer crosses as a COPY OF THE POINTEE, judged by the pointee's type (DEF-360 relaxed): sites 4-6, the
// owner pointee, stay NITPICK-BORROW-004 (the message names `(move(<-p)).m()` into a `move` receiver); landing 169's
// sites 14-16, PLAIN DATA through a pointer local with the owner writing, with nothing written and through an
// inline address, are legal -- the legal half's controls 21-23 read the right value. Sites 14-16 are now a POINTEE
// WHOSE TYPE HOLDS AN ADDRESS, `H{ p: @d }` behind the pointer, in the same three spellings: the copy carries the
// address, a borrow crossing the spawn, NITPICK-BORROW-004 at the receiver -- refused on 169 by the blanket rule,
// silent 114/114 at both legs under the relaxation's first cut, which judged ownership alone (DEF-364's shape
// reached through a pointer; wt/51a/.internal/probes/t170/pre8/ x1-x3); the AWAIT of it is the legal half's
// control 27.
// LANDING 172 (2026-10-30): the review of 321f31f's two faces. A by-value RECEIVER that holds a borrow -- `H{ p: @d }`
// as `self` -- crossed a spawn unrefused, where the argument twin `drop rdf(h)` was `-004`: `escape_spawn_recv` ran
// the receiver's walk and threw its verdict away (DEF-364; f1a, f1b: the task read the owner's rewritten string,
// 114/114 at both legs on 169, 170 and 171). Now the walk's verdict is judged as an argument's is (sites 17-20, named and
// inline, with `d` rewritten and with nothing written: NITPICK-BORROW-004 at the receiver). And DEF-361 read the
// TOP-LEVEL kind alone, so a type that holds a type parameter by value -- `T?`, a generic struct's instance `Bx<T>`,
// `T[2]`, `Result<T>`, a generic enum's instance `Op2<T>`, `Bx<T>?` -- crossed a spawn by value from a generic body
// instantiated at `string` (DEF-365); now `spawn_type_holds_param` answers YES for a `T`, `Self` or associated type
// held in storage, through an element, a payload or a type argument, and the by-value rule refuses it unless the
// parameter is `move` (sites 21-26: `-004` at the argument). No wrong value was measured for DEF-365 (its cells ran
// 0/0 at both legs on 170, wt/51a/.internal/probes/t171/def365/): the closed rule's gap. The `Self` and
// associated-type faces are tests/analysis/rejection/spawn_self_assoc_byval.npk, alone in their file because each
// waits on a frontend change (DEF-376, DEF-377); site 25's generic enum instance cannot be BUILT yet (DEF-375, the
// emitter), and this file is the checker's. Landing 171's checker reports none of sites 17-26. Site 2 keeps its one
// report, the -015: the walk gives the byte read through the live view `v` the verdict of the byte's TYPE, which holds
// no address (DEF-378's first face, fixed in this landing), so DEF-364 does not refuse the receiver. Landing 171's
// build 2 judged the walk's verdict before that type gate and refused the receiver here too, as it refused the legal
// receivers of wt/51a/.internal/probes/t171/p364/ o1, o2, o7 and o8, whose ARGUMENT twins o1a, o2a, o7a and o8a
// landing 170 and landing 171 refuse -- each legal now (tests/backend/programs/escape_verdicts_ok.npk).
mod:spawn_review_faces;
error:E1;
fixed Duration:J2 = Duration{ ns: 2000000000i64 };
struct:W = { int64:k; };
struct:SS = { string:s; int64:k; };
struct:PD = { int64:k; };
struct:H = { string->:p; };
struct:Bx<T> = { T:v; };
enum:Op2<T> = { Some(T); None; };
impl:W = {
    thread async func:look = NIL(W:self) joins J2 {
        await sleep(raw duration_ms(1i64)) ?| NIL;
        if (self.k != 104i64) { fail E1; }
        pass NIL;
    };
};
impl:PD = {
    thread async func:lookp = NIL(PD:self) joins J2 {
        await sleep(raw duration_ms(1i64)) ?| NIL;
        if (self.k != 1i64) { fail E1; }
        pass NIL;
    };
};
impl:SS = {
    thread async func:looks = NIL(SS:self) joins J2 {
        await sleep(raw duration_ms(1i64)) ?| NIL;
        fixed uint8[]:xb = string_bytes(self.s);
        if (xb[0i64] != 97u8) { fail E1; }
        pass NIL;
    };
};
impl:H = {
    async func:rd = NIL(H:self) {
        await sleep(raw duration_ms(1i64)) ?| NIL;
        fixed uint8[]:xb = string_bytes(<-self.p);
        if (xb[0i64] != 104u8) { fail E1; }
        pass NIL;
    };
};
thread async func:filler = NIL(shared_arena<int64>->:s) joins J2 {
    await sleep(raw duration_ms(1i64)) ?| NIL;
    Handle<int64>:h = s.alloc(424242i64);
    int64:v = s.get(h) ?! E1;
    if (v != 424242i64) { fail E1; }
    pass NIL;
};
thread async func:peekg<T> = NIL(T:x) joins J2 { await sleep(raw duration_ms(1i64)) ?| NIL; pass NIL; };
thread async func:peekc<T: Copy> = NIL(T:x) joins J2 { await sleep(raw duration_ms(1i64)) ?| NIL; pass NIL; };
thread async func:peeko<T> = NIL(T?:x) joins J2 { await sleep(raw duration_ms(1i64)) ?| NIL; pass NIL; };
thread async func:peekb<T> = NIL(Bx<T>:x) joins J2 { await sleep(raw duration_ms(1i64)) ?| NIL; pass NIL; };
thread async func:peeka<T> = NIL(T[2]:x) joins J2 { await sleep(raw duration_ms(1i64)) ?| NIL; pass NIL; };
thread async func:peekr<T> = NIL(Result<T>:x) joins J2 { await sleep(raw duration_ms(1i64)) ?| NIL; pass NIL; };
thread async func:peekn<T> = NIL(Op2<T>:x) joins J2 { await sleep(raw duration_ms(1i64)) ?| NIL; pass NIL; };
thread async func:peekq<T> = NIL(Bx<T>?:x) joins J2 { await sleep(raw duration_ms(1i64)) ?| NIL; pass NIL; };
func:mkres<T> = T(move T:a) {
    return Result{value: move(a)};
};
trait:Tr = { async func:m = NIL(Self:self, move int64:n); };
impl:SS:Tr = {
    thread async func:m = NIL(SS:self, move int64:n) joins J2 {
        await sleep(raw duration_ms(1i64)) ?| NIL;
        fixed uint8[]:xb = string_bytes(self.s);
        if (xb[0i64] != 97u8) { fail E1; }
        if (n != 5i64) { fail E1; }
        pass NIL;
    };
};
trait:Tr2 = { async func:m2 = NIL(Self:self, move string:n); };
impl:SS:Tr2 = {
    thread async func:m2 = NIL(SS:self, move string:n) joins J2 {
        await sleep(raw duration_ms(1i64)) ?| NIL;
        fixed uint8[]:xb = string_bytes(self.s);
        if (xb[0i64] != 97u8) { fail E1; }
        if (n.len != 3i64) { fail E1; }
        pass NIL;
    };
};
trait:Tp = { async func:mp = NIL(Self->:self); };
impl:W:Tp = {
    thread async func:mp = NIL(W->:self) joins J2 {
        await sleep(raw duration_ms(1i64)) ?| NIL;
        if (self.k == 999i64) { fail E1; }
        pass NIL;
    };
};

// --- DEF-359: THE RECEIVER AND THE SANCTIONED ARGUMENT ARE WALKED -----------------------------------
// 1. the pick expression IS the spawned method's receiver; its arm views `d` and rewrites it (f1a)
async func:recv_is_pick = NIL() {
    string:d = string_concat("hello", " world");
    {
        drop (pick (1i32) { (*) {
            fixed uint8[]:v = string_bytes(d);
            d = string_concat("xyzzy", "!");
            if (v[0i64] != 104u8) { fail E1; }
            give W{ k: 104i64 }; } }).look();
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// 2. the pick inside a struct-literal receiver, the viewed byte carried into the task (f1b)
async func:recv_struct_literal_pick = NIL() {
    string:d = string_concat("hello", " world");
    {
        drop (W{ k: (pick (1i32) { (*) {
            fixed uint8[]:v = string_bytes(d);
            d = string_concat("xyzzy", "!");
            give (v[0i64] => int64); } }) }).look();
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// 3. the pick inside a SANCTIONED pointer argument, a `shared_arena<int64>->` given out of the arm (f1c)
async func:sanctioned_arg_pick = NIL() {
    shared_arena<int64>:s = shared_arena_make(8i64);
    shared_arena<int64>->:sp = @s;
    string:d = string_concat("hello", " world");
    {
        drop filler(pick (1i32) { (*) {
            fixed uint8[]:v = string_bytes(d);
            d = string_concat("xyzzy", "!");
            if (v[0i64] != 104u8) { fail E1; }
            give sp; } });
    }
    s.destroy();
    pass NIL;
};

// --- DEF-360: A BY-VALUE RECEIVER THROUGH A POINTER IS THE POINTEE ---------------------------------
// 4. a by-value `self` method spawned through a POINTER local, the owner rewriting under the task (f2a)
async func:byval_self_through_pointer = NIL() {
    SS:w = SS{ s: string_concat("ab", "c"), k: 1i64 };
    SS->:p = @w;
    {
        drop p.looks();
        p.s = string_concat("zz", "z");
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// 5. the same through an inline address, `drop (@w).looks()` (f2b)
async func:byval_self_through_address = NIL() {
    SS:w = SS{ s: string_concat("ab", "c"), k: 1i64 };
    {
        drop (@w).looks();
        w.s = string_concat("zz", "z");
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// 6. through the pointer, the owner writing NOTHING: the copy is the hazard (direction (A), as m12)
async func:byval_self_through_pointer_no_write = NIL() {
    SS:w = SS{ s: string_concat("ab", "c"), k: 1i64 };
    SS->:p = @w;
    {
        drop p.looks();
    }
    if (w.k != 1i64) { fail E1; }
    pass NIL;
};

// --- DEF-361: A TYPE PARAMETER IS AN OWNER TO THE BY-VALUE RULE -------------------------------------
// 7. a generic `T` local handed to a by-value `T:x` parameter, the local re-assigned under the task (f3a)
async func:generic_byval_named<T> = NIL(move T:a, move T:c) {
    T:l = move(a);
    {
        drop peekg::<T>(l);
        l = move(c);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// 8. `move(a)` of a `move T` parameter into a BY-VALUE `T:x`: the parameter's mode decides, not the spelling (f3c)
async func:generic_byval_moved<T> = NIL(move T:a) {
    {
        drop peekg::<T>(move(a));
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// 9. a `T: Copy` instance by value -- a licensed copy (D-327), refused here because the escape pass reaches no
//    bound table: KNOWN, the relaxation owed (0 tree sites by the sweep)
async func:generic_copy_byval<T: Copy> = NIL(T:a) {
    {
        drop peekc::<T>(a);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// --- DEF-362: A QUALIFIER IS NO RECEIVER -------------------------------------------------------------
// 10. `drop Tr.m(w, 5i64)`: `w` is parameter 0's by-value `Self:self`, the owner rewriting under the task (f4a)
async func:trait_qualified_owner = NIL() {
    SS:w = SS{ s: string_concat("ab", "c"), k: 1i64 };
    {
        drop Tr.m(w, 5i64);
        w.s = string_concat("zz", "z");
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// 11. a TEMPORARY owner as the trait-qualified receiver, dead at the statement's end (f4b; oi5's class)
async func:trait_qualified_temporary = NIL() {
    {
        drop Tr.m(SS{ s: string_concat("ab", "c"), k: 1i64 }, 5i64);
        string:junk = string_concat("qq", "q");
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// 12. `drop Tr2.m2(w, move(s2))`: `w` refused ALONE -- the `move` argument beside it is legal (f4c; landing
//     168 refused `move(s2)` and admitted `w`)
async func:trait_qualified_both_faces = NIL() {
    SS:w = SS{ s: string_concat("ab", "c"), k: 1i64 };
    string:s2 = string_concat("ab", "c");
    {
        drop Tr2.m2(w, move(s2));
        w.s = string_concat("zz", "z");
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// 13. a trait-qualified spawn with a POINTER receiver, `drop Tp.mp(@w)`: the address is argument 0 and crosses
//     as `drop w.mp()`'s receiver does (D-180)
async func:trait_qualified_pointer_receiver = NIL() {
    W:w = W{ k: 1i64 };
    {
        drop Tp.mp(@w);
        w = W{ k: 2i64 };
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// --- LANDING 170: A POINTEE WHOSE TYPE HOLDS AN ADDRESS ----------------------------------------------
// 14. `H{ p: @d }` behind `H->:hp`, `drop hp.rd()`, `d` rewritten under the task: the copy of the pointee
//     carries the address (x1: 114/114 at both legs on 168 and under the relaxation's first cut)
async func:holds_address_through_pointer = NIL() {
    string:d = string_concat("hello", " world");
    H:h = H{ p: @d };
    H->:hp = @h;
    {
        drop hp.rd();
        d = string_concat("xyzzy", "!");
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// 15. the same with NOTHING written: a borrow crossing is refused whatever the owner does (x3, as site 6)
async func:holds_address_through_pointer_no_write = NIL() {
    string:d = string_concat("hello", " world");
    H:h = H{ p: @d };
    H->:hp = @h;
    {
        drop hp.rd();
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// 16. through an inline address, `drop (@h).rd()`, `d` rewritten under the task (x2)
async func:holds_address_through_address = NIL() {
    string:d = string_concat("hello", " world");
    H:h = H{ p: @d };
    {
        drop (@h).rd();
        d = string_concat("xyzzy", "!");
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// --- LANDING 172: A RECEIVER THAT HOLDS A BORROW (DEF-364) ------------------------------------------------
// 17. a by-value receiver HOLDING A BORROW, by name: `H{ p: @d }` as `self`, `d` rewritten under the task (f1a)
async func:recv_holds_named = NIL() {
    string:d = string_concat("hello", " world");
    H:h = H{ p: @d };
    {
        drop h.rd();
        d = string_concat("xyzzy", "!");
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// 18. the same receiver INLINE, a struct literal (f1b)
async func:recv_holds_inline = NIL() {
    string:d = string_concat("hello", " world");
    {
        drop (H{ p: @d }).rd();
        d = string_concat("xyzzy", "!");
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// 19. by name with NOTHING written: a borrow crossing is refused whatever the owner does (f1d)
async func:recv_holds_named_no_write = NIL() {
    string:d = string_concat("hello", " world");
    H:h = H{ p: @d };
    {
        drop h.rd();
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// 20. inline with nothing written (f1f)
async func:recv_holds_inline_no_write = NIL() {
    string:d = string_concat("hello", " world");
    {
        drop (H{ p: @d }).rd();
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// --- LANDING 172: A TYPE THAT HOLDS A TYPE PARAMETER BY VALUE (DEF-365) ----------------------------------------
// 21. `T?`, the owner re-assigned under the task (f2a)
async func:generic_opt_byval<T> = NIL(move T:a, move T:c) {
    T?:o = move(a);
    {
        drop peeko::<T>(o);
        o = move(c);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// 22. a generic struct's instance, `Bx<T>` (f2d)
async func:generic_box_byval<T> = NIL(move T:a, move T:c) {
    Bx<T>:b = Bx{ v: move(a) };
    {
        drop peekb::<T>(b);
        b = Bx{ v: move(c) };
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// 23. an array, `T[2]` (t171/def365/f2f)
async func:generic_array_byval<T> = NIL(move T:a, move T:b, move T:c, move T:d) {
    T[2]:o = [move(a), move(b)];
    {
        drop peeka::<T>(o);
        o = [move(c), move(d)];
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// 24. a `Result<T>` (f2g)
async func:generic_result_byval<T> = NIL(move T:a, move T:c) {
    Result<T>:o = mkres::<T>(move(a));
    {
        drop peekr::<T>(o);
        o = mkres::<T>(move(c));
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// 25. a generic enum's instance, `Op2<T>` (f2j; DEF-375: the emitter cannot build it in a generic body yet)
async func:generic_enum_byval<T> = NIL(move T:a, move T:c) {
    Op2<T>:o = Op2.Some(move(a));
    {
        drop peekn::<T>(o);
        o = Op2.Some(move(c));
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// 26. nested, `Bx<T>?` (f2k)
async func:generic_nested_byval<T> = NIL(move T:a, move T:c) {
    Bx<T>?:o = Bx{ v: move(a) };
    {
        drop peekq::<T>(o);
        o = Bx{ v: move(c) };
    }
    pass NIL;
};

async func:main = int32(cstring[]:_~argv) {
    await recv_is_pick() ?| NIL;
    await recv_struct_literal_pick() ?| NIL;
    await sanctioned_arg_pick() ?| NIL;
    await byval_self_through_pointer() ?| NIL;
    await byval_self_through_address() ?| NIL;
    await byval_self_through_pointer_no_write() ?| NIL;
    await generic_byval_named::<string>(string_concat("ab", "c"), string_concat("de", "f")) ?| NIL;
    await generic_byval_moved::<string>(string_concat("ab", "c")) ?| NIL;
    await generic_copy_byval::<int64>(7i64) ?| NIL;
    await trait_qualified_owner() ?| NIL;
    await trait_qualified_temporary() ?| NIL;
